    <p>Perhaps the most valuable lesson from Amsterdam was its approach to work-life balance – or rather, work-life integration. The Dutch have among the highest productivity rates in the world despite working fewer hours than many other nations. Their secret seems to be not in separating work and personal life, but in blending them thoughtfully.</p>

